---
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SENDER } from "../../shared/site";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "27 October 2026";
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How Headmesh collects, uses and protects your personal information." ogImage="privacy">
  <article class="container-page pt-16 sm:pt-24">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        headmesh.dev is run by {SENDER.legalName} ("we"). This policy explains what personal information the site
        collects, why, and what you can do about it. We collect as little as we can.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <h3>When you join the waitlist</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address;</li>
        <li>what you'd use Headmesh for, if you tell us;</li>
        <li>
          a record of your consent: the version of the wording you agreed to, when you signed up, when you confirmed and,
          if it happens, when you unsubscribed;
        </li>
        <li>where you came from, such as the referring website or campaign tags (<code>utm_source</code> and similar);</li>
        <li>a keyed hash of your IP address, used only to stop abuse. We don't store the IP address itself.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When you visit any page</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Spam protection.</strong> The waitlist form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks signals from your
          browser to tell people from bots.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views without cookies and
          without identifying you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Delivery.</strong> Requests pass through Cloudflare's network, which protects the site, and reach
          our server, which logs them briefly for security and troubleshooting. Both see request data such as IP
          addresses.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies. If you pick a light or dark theme, that choice is kept in your browser's local
        storage and never sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to send you a confirmation email, and then early-access invitations and occasional Headmesh updates;</li>
        <li>to understand, in aggregate, who wants Headmesh and what for;</li>
        <li>to prevent spam and abuse of the waitlist.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don't sell your information, use it for advertising or share it with anyone except the providers below.</p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>We rely on three providers, who process data for us under their own security and privacy commitments:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Hetzner</strong> runs the server in Germany that hosts the site and stores the waitlist
          (<a href="https://www.hetzner.com/legal/privacy-policy/">Hetzner privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> protects and speeds up the site and runs Turnstile and Web Analytics
          (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Resend</strong> delivers our emails (<a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend privacy policy</a>).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers store or process your information outside Canada: in the European Union (the server) and the
        United States (Cloudflare and Resend). There it may be accessible to authorities under local law.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep waitlist information until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it, and we delete sign-ups that were never
        confirmed. After you unsubscribe we keep only what we need to honour that choice and to show we had your
        consent: your email address and the consent dates.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Unsubscribe at any time with the link in any email we send. We act on it immediately.</li>
        <li>
          Ask to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you by emailing <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
          We'll reply within 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you're not happy with our answer, you can complain to the
          <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Everything is sent over HTTPS. Access to the waitlist database is limited to the people who run Headmesh, and our
        links and logs never include your email address.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we'll update the date at the top. If a change affects how we use information you've
        already given us, we'll email you first.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {SENDER.legalName}{SENDER.postalAddress && <>, {SENDER.postalAddress}</>} · Email <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
